The Early Years
Our English teachers are keenly aware of the importance of teaching the children to read well and develop their literacy skills. It is a vital part of our curriculum and the children learn how to express themselves in different ways through reading, writing, speaking and listening as they progress towards their end of year exams.
In Key Stage 1, we teach children to read using phonics at home and encourage them to use this skill when reading for pleasure. The children are encouraged to make links between words and images so that they can be drawn on to new vocabulary. We have also developed learning packs which provide varied activities to help children get the most out of lessons. These resources will continue to support your child’s development throughout their time at school and beyond.
The Early Years Foundation Stage (EYFS) curriculum encompasses the areas of communication, language, maths, science, geography and social studies. The EYFS aims to ensure that all children:
- Develop essential knowledge and understanding of all subjects including the A-Levels;
- Develop a lifelong love of reading;
- Explore and relate to other cultures and peoples around the world;
